# demesne-sync.exclude — the ONE exclusion set, shared by both directions of
# demesne-sync.sh (the rsync that copies, and the `diff -r` identity gate).
# dotfiles-lg1z.
#
# WHY ONE FILE. The gate is only meaningful if it is blind to EXACTLY what the
# sync declines to copy. Two hand-maintained lists drift, and the drift is
# silent in the worst direction: an exclusion the sync honours but the gate does
# not means the gate can NEVER read empty (the state lg1z was filed for — a bare
# `diff -r` reported 96 entries, most of them bytecode). The reverse — an
# exclusion the gate honours but the sync does not — means real content is
# copied into the private repo while the gate looks away from it. So the script
# reads this file once and derives both `rsync --exclude=` and `diff -x` from
# the same lines.
#
# FORMAT. One pattern per line. `#` starts a comment; blank lines ignored.
# Patterns are BASENAME globs with no `/` — that form means the same thing to
# rsync (a pattern with no slash matches the basename at any depth) and to
# `diff -x` (fnmatch against the basename). Do not add a pattern containing a
# slash: the two tools do NOT agree on those, and the script rejects them.
#
# THE BAR FOR ADDING ONE. Every entry here is a hole in the gate. A pattern must
# name something that is GENERATED — reproducible from tracked content by a
# build/test run — never something merely large or merely private. The script
# refuses to run if any pattern here matches a git-TRACKED path component in the
# source, which is the mechanical form of that bar.

# --- verified present in the live source tree, 2026-08-09 -----------------
# Counted before this list existed: `diff -r` over agents/ refs/ claude/ with no
# exclusions returned 96 entries; with these six it returned 89 real ones — the
# seven suppressed were all python bytecode and test-runner caches. Every one of
# these is already gitignored in BOTH repos.
__pycache__
.ruff_cache
.pytest_cache
node_modules
*.pyc
.DS_Store

# --- pre-emptive, same class, not currently present ------------------------
# Python/JS toolchain siblings of the six above. None exist in the source tree
# today (verified by `find` over agents/ refs/ claude/, 2026-08-09); they are
# listed because the day one appears is a day the gate would otherwise go red
# for a reason that is not drift. Each is a name that can never be legitimate
# brain content.
.mypy_cache
.tox
.venv
*.egg-info
